[en.C11_DESC]
After the Ultimate Battle, Queen Chrysalis returned to the long-lost changeling hive and re-established the authoritarian rule. Queen Chrysalis forced the changelings to return to their unhatched state and promised that the changelings would never be hungry again.\n\nQueen Chrysalis believes that she is an excellent ruler, and the purpose of everything she does is not her own desire for power, or at least not all of it, but the strong future of the Changelings. Now, the Changelings will finally surpass those inferior ponies and become the master race of Equestria.\n\nBut it is ironic that she soon found that in this world she had destroyed with her own power, it became increasingly difficult to be a good leader... Creatures were so indifferent to each other that she found it difficult to find enough “love” to fill the hungry stomachs of her subjects.\n\nWhen rumors can no longer be squashed by iron hooves, when the ambitious and the seditious depart from the shadows, chaos will rise.

[en.PIHC_WS_C11_desc]
In the spring of the year 1000, the Queen Chrysalis, who returned victorious in the Ultimate Battle, ordered the changelings to return to their original forms and launched a large-scale retaliation within the changeling community. In this action, the leader Thorax became the first changeling to be publicly hanged in front of the hive.\nHowever, a solid rule is not possible to maintain only through fear and killing. Queen Chrysalis naturally understands this, and she truly believes that changelings will have a better life under her reign.\nTherefore, Queen Chrysalis promised to the changelings who returned to their original forms: by “plundering” the love of other races instead of “sharing”, changelings will get far more love than they used to.\nAt the same time, Queen Chrysalis turned her spearhead to the ponies: for a long time, the ponies have been the dominant race over the entire Equestria world. Now, Queen Chrysalis declared to the world that changelings are the true master race. Changelings will use their sharp teeth and claws to fight for their lebensraum.\n“Changelings Master Race!” This rousing slogan successfully persuaded most of the changelings who were otherwise still skeptical and fearful. In the autumn of the year 1000, all the dissenters among the changelings had been arrested, exiled, or physically eliminated. To fulfill her promise, Queen Chrysalis led the reorganized changeling army on a conquering expedition to the Crystal Empire.\n\nWell, apparently, the military ability of the Queen of Chrysalis is not better than her political means. She may be a tactical genius, but obviously does not understand long-term strategy: invading a country in the far north in the autumn, it seems to be a bad decision.\nIn the winter of 1000, the joint army led by the Queen of Chrysalis suffered heavy losses in the winter offensive, which also intensified her internal conflicts with the Warm Light Flow, and caused the Queen of Chrysalis to lose the dominance of the Crystal Empire’s conquest war. In the summer of 1000, perhaps benefiting from the weather, the summer offensive commanded by Cozy Glow was successful, and the army advanced to the Crystal City. Although it was a tragic victory, Cozy and Chrysalis took the opportunity to negotiate with the Crystal Empire, claiming to have conquered the Crystal Empire, sort of.\nThe failure of the winter offensive weakened the Queen of Chrysalis’s bargaining base, and she had to temporarily abandon the discriminatory rhetoric against the entire pony race. Instead, she and Cozy targeted the crystal ponies together, which gave the Empire of Equestria a lot of benefits in the affairs of the Crystal Empire. In the subsequent Canterlot Pact negotiations, this also became the main contradiction between Cozy Glow and the Queen of Chrysalis, ultimately leading to the signing of the Canterlot Pact being delayed for several days.\nAlthough the results were not satisfactory, at least the Queen of Chrysalis fulfilled her promise - according to the Crystal Empire Ceasefire and the Canterlot Pact, the Crystal Empire began to provide love offerings to the Changelings, and the Changelings were happy to see the living of a prosperous life - although it seemed not as long as imagined.\n\n“Plunder” is indeed the fastest way to obtain love. Through more efficient and organized “plunder”, the Changelings seem to have really obtained much more love than “sharing”, and live a happier life. But “sharing” can create love out of nothing, while “plunder” can never be stopped - as the love of the Crystal Empire itself begins to decrease and even become scarce, the dark clouds will once again shroud the future of the Changelings.\nQueen Chrysalis believes that she is an excellent ruler, and the purpose of everything she does is not her own desire for power, or at least not all of it, but the strong future of the Changelings. But it is ironic that she soon found that in this world she had destroyed with her own power, it became increasingly difficult to be a good leader...

